from `git diff` for a submodule ignored by `.gitmodules`, a submodule with uncommitted content, symlinks and a directory replaced by a file, unmerged entries, a POSE root below the repository top, intent-to-add, staged-then-reverted changes and a range base. They were withdrawn: the callers run their original `git diff` again, reading the index through a `memfd` (D1). `TestReadOnlyIndexDiffAnswersAsThePlainDiff` builds those states and requires each read to answer byte for byte as the plain diff, leave `.git/index` identical and leave no lock; it also runs the review history ledger's diff (N9). Each guard fails its test mutated out.\n - 2026-11-26: review round 2 (rrn-233e9d0e27a7230a) requested changes. N10: the memfd carried a new time, so a racily clean entry was trusted on its stat and a real change was hidden; the memfd (and the copy outside Linux) now keeps the index's modification time, and `TestReadOnlyIndexDiffSeesARacilyCleanEntry` fails with the current time in its place. N11: without an index file the read runs plainly instead of failing, and `check` applies the read-only index to its diff only (`TestValidationReadsAnswerWithoutAnIndex` fails with the missing-index case removed; the diff-only restriction is behaviour-preserving, as `ls-files` never writes, and has no test of its own). N13: scope selection keeps the cause of a failed read, and the index read reports its own error. N12 is a follow-up.\n - 2026-11-26: review round 3 requested changes with follow-ups only (N14–N17), because its sandbox rerun of `validate` failed for environment reasons and was recorded `failed`. N17: the index is checked and read through one open file within the bound. N14–N16 are follow-ups.\n+- 2026-11-26: review round 4 (rrn-282d73ecd35bcc64) raised follow-ups only and requested changes for its failed sandbox `validate`, as round 3 did. N21: a FIFO or device at the index path is refused before it is opened, and the opened file must be the one checked (`TestReadOnlyIndexRefusesAFIFOIndex` blocks with the check removed). N18–N20 are the recorded follow-ups.\n \n ### Results summary\n The full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n \n ### Requirement trace\n-- R1 [satisfied] test:TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone, test:TestReadOnlyIndexDiffAnswersAsThePlainDiff, test:TestReadOnlyIndexDiffSeesARacilyCleanEntry, test:TestValidationReadsAnswerWithoutAnIndex\n+- R1 [satisfied] test:TestReadOnlyIndexRefusesAFIFOIndex, test:TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone, test:TestReadOnlyIndexDiffAnswersAsThePlainDiff, test:TestReadOnlyIndexDiffSeesARacilyCleanEntry, test:TestValidationReadsAnswerWithoutAnIndex\n - R2 [satisfied] test:TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone\n - R3 [satisfied] test:TestConcurrentValidationReadsNeverChangeTheIndex\n \ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\nindex f277a7c3..32e6b681 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\n@@ -29,21 +29,26 @@ func ReadOnlyIndex(cmd *exec.Cmd, root string) (func(), error) {\n \t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s cannot be located: %w\", root, err)\n \t}\n \tpath := strings.TrimSuffix(string(out), \"\\n\")\n-\tif _, err := os.Lstat(path); os.IsNotExist(err) {\n+\tbefore, err := os.Stat(path)\n+\tif os.IsNotExist(err) {\n \t\t// No index yet: there is no stat cache to refresh, so the plain read\n \t\t// writes nothing (review round 2, N11).\n \t\treturn func() {}, nil\n \t}\n-\t// One open file is checked and read, within the bound (review round 3,\n-\t// N17): a file swapped in between cannot escape it.\n+\t// A FIFO or device is refused before it is opened, which could block\n+\t// (review round 4, N21); the open file must be the file checked, and is\n+\t// read within the bound (round 3, N17).\n+\tif err != nil || !before.Mode().IsRegular() {\n+\t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s is not a regular file\", root)\n+\t}\n \tf, err := os.Open(path)\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s cannot be read: %w\", root, err)\n \t}\n \tdefer f.Close()\n \tinfo, err := f.Stat()\n-\tif err != nil || !info.Mode().IsRegular() {\n-\t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s is not a regular file\", root)\n+\tif err != nil || !info.Mode().IsRegular() || !os.SameFile(before, info) {\n+\t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s changed while it was opened\", root)\n \t}\n \traw, err := io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(f, diffIndexLimit+1))\n \tif err != nil {\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go\nindex 4f071acb..f3fe6224 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go\n@@ -5,6 +5,8 @@ import (\n \t\"os\"\n \t\"os/exec\"\n \t\"path/filepath\"\n+\t\"runtime\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n \t\"testing\"\n \t\"time\"\n )\n@@ -182,3 +184,33 @@ func TestReadOnlyIndexDiffSeesARacilyCleanEntry(t *testing.T) {\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"a racily clean change was hidden: %q\", got)\n \t}\n }\n+\n+// Review round 4, N21: a FIFO at the index path is refused, not opened,\n+// which would block.\n+func TestReadOnlyIndexRefusesAFIFOIndex(t *testing.T) {\n+\tif runtime.GOOS == \"windows\" {\n+\t\tt.Skip(\"no FIFOs\")\n+\t}\n+\troot := t.TempDir()\n+\tif out, err := exec.Command(\"git\", \"-C\", root, \"init\", \"-q\").CombinedOutput(); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err, string(out))\n+\t}\n+\tindex := filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index\")\n+\t_ = os.Remove(index)\n+\tif out, err := exec.Command(\"mkfifo\", index).CombinedOutput(); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Skip(\"mkfifo unavailable:\", err, string(out))\n+\t}\n+\tdone := make(chan error, 1)\n+\tgo func() {\n+\t\t_, err := RawGitDiffReadOnly(root, \"-C\", root, \"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"--\")\n+\t\tdone <- err\n+\t}()\n+\tselect {\n+\tcase err := <-done:\n+\t\tif err == nil || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"not a regular file\") {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a FIFO index: %v\", err)\n+\t\t}\n+\tcase <-time.After(10 * time.Second):\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"reading a FIFO index blocked\")\n+\t}\n+}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"28c03782-5455-43e8-9fe5-fc4c4b906e6d","timestamp":"2026-11-26T20:27:49.819Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"ok  \tgithub.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/cli\t1.804s\nok  \tgithub.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/pose\t1.202s\n .pose/indexes/delivery-integrity.json              |  848 ++---\n .pose/indexes/generation.json                      |   12 +-\n .pose/indexes/spec-graph.json                      | 1172 +++----\n .pose/results/delivery-validation.json             |  944 +++---\n .pose/results/vread-binding.md                     |    1 +\n .../e4de37058767b545dae9b88a/000001.json           |   11 +\n .../e4de37058767b545dae9b88a/000001.result.json    |    6 +\n .../review-attestations/rva-f98437367746e925.json  |  237 ++\n .pose/review-bundles/rvb-80a3d391176eb7fe.json     | 3505 ++++++++++++++++++++\n .pose/review-conclusions/rrn-282d73ecd35bcc64.json |   13 +\n .pose/review-run-ledger/rrn-282d73ecd35bcc64.json  |    8 +\n ...eeb1779194777691ac98c9c4b05a1f27a66359f4cb.json |   23 +\n .../review-runs/rrn-282d73ecd35bcc64.events.ndjson |   30 +\n .pose/review-runs/rrn-282d73ecd35bcc64.json        |  144 +\n .pose/review-runs/rrn-282d73ecd35bcc64.transcript  |  152 +\n ...23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md |    3 +-\n pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go       |   15 +-\n pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go  |   32 +\n 18 files changed, 5665 insertions(+), 1491 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md\nindex b45ef22f..64e6547f 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose